      "q": "6. Using a Punnett square, work out the distribution of phenotypic features in the first filial generation after a cross between a homozygous female and a heterozygous male for a single locus.",
      "a": "When heterozygous male guinea pigs $(W w)$ with black coats are crossed with homozygous female guinea pigs $(w w)$ with white coats, we can see that the male generates two types of gametes $W$ and $w$, while the female produces only one form of gamete $w$.\nWe can see that the genotypic and phenotypic ratios in the $(F 1)$ generations are the same, i.e., $1: 1$, using the Punnett square."
