      "q": "9. What is primary productivity, and what factors influence it?",
      "a": "Primary productivity refers to the organic matter produced by producers per unit area over time. Environmental factors like light, temperature, water, and precipitation, along with nutrient availability and plant access for photosynthesis, determine an ecosystem's primary productivity."
